    "description": "Developed an orchestration service to manage eBPF programs on Linux virtual machines in Azure Data Centers. The service includes a Service CLI, Backend Service, and Control Agent running on the target VM to emit Prometheus metrics with data collected from eBPF maps.\n\nDeveloped and implemented a stress test framework for Azure Media Services, based on requirements gathered from all feature teams.\n\nDeveloped and implemented a plug-in model testing framework to monitor the real-time health of Azure Media Services in all Azure regions. This framework included advanced logging and alerting capabilities. The new system significantly enhanced the previous version by resolving all framework issues and enabling direct alerts to feature teams, thereby improving the efficiency of incident handling.\n\nDeveloped and executed big data processing pipelines on a Spark cluster to handle inventory data from Azure Data Centers globally.\n\nDeveloped and deployed a distributed platform to gather information on network-connected devices across all Microsoft Azure Data Centers.\n\nDeveloped and executed WMIBridge to facilitate communication between WMI clients and CSPs (COM components for Device Management) on Windows. This innovation removed the need for CSP owners to create additional interfaces for Windows applications.\n\nEnhanced engineering efficiencies by developing an automated C++ source generation system from XML files for WMI providers (as part of WMIBridge), and integrating it into the build process.\n\nDeveloped and incorporated the MDM Local Management library into the Windows SDK, facilitating MDM management scenarios without the need for a server.\n\nDeveloped a test framework for WLAN driver verification, ensuring quality in vendors' wireless device drivers as part of the Windows logo program.\n\nStreamlined the WLAN testing environment by incorporating the SoftAP filter driver into the test framework, thereby eliminating the need for a physical AP during test execution.",
